{"body":{"text":["*Awaiting the author's ratification. Unlike the briefs around it, Keeping the field and its Elevation are written as the work is now to be done, and are marked ratified once he has read and accepted them (23/152).*"]},"id":"1M89KKND7DD5000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A question is held in the field as a statement whose status is open: \"if something is a question, make it. In the substrate.\" (10/8). The threads raised before the elevation stay in the field until the sessions are drawn anew, and are no part of the work. What a session did is committed before it ends, and no session starts on another's uncommitted work: \"We never want to start off a session with local changes.\" (4/2)."]},"id":"1M89KKND7DD5001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Threads, paths and cycles go once the sessions are drawn anew: \"Yes, threads and paths are let go, but so is more things, cycles, etc.\" (23/110). Condensations and measures go with them on the session's list, which he did not contest (23/111), though he once thought measures might be a dimension of their own (23/52). Statistics and their board stay, an idea the interface was not ready for (23/52). Glass's values, sovereignty and one source of truth among them, \"ought to be a brief somewhere anyway, probably\" (23/62), and wait for that brief. Until the redraw, what goes stays in the field as it is, and is no part of the work."]},"id":"1M89KKND7DD5002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Stale. Written before the elevation, the design still points at threads and paths as the home of open questions; it is to be rewritten whole once the elevation is done (23/152).*"]},"id":"1M89KKND7DD5003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
